d 'DVAR': module to perform Distributional VAR, multimodality and distributional impulse responses
d
d  dvar implements the distributional vector autoregression of
d Wang, Oka and Zhu (2025, Journal of Applied Econometrics). The
d conditional joint distribution of a vector time series is
d factorised into univariate conditional distributions, each
d estimated by distribution regression (logit/probit, with the
d optional elastic net of the authors' replication code), with
d sandwich/HAC inference (Theorem 1), rearrangement, sequential
d sampling, local-projection multi-step distributions,
d distributional / quantile / moment impulse responses with a
d moving-block bootstrap, and out-of-sample PIT (Rossi-Sekhposyan),
d CRPS, quantile- and log-score evaluation. The subcommand -dvar
d kernel- implements the kernel estimator and density impulse
d responses of Adrian, Boyarchenko and Giannone (2021,
d International Economic Review). Joint densities are drawn as
d Parula heat maps / contours, and the number of modes is reported. d
d KW: distributional VAR
d KW: kernel estimator
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261126
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
